        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Opportunity Prioritization Assessment"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770269197917"
          },
          "code": "OPPORTUNITY_PRIORITIZATION_ASSESSMENT",
          "id": "1769619779382",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769619779385_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Goal: Calculate a numeric prioritization score (0–100) and a classification (Low, Medium, High, Critical) for an opportunity using the provided PRIORITIZATION_RULES and extracted signals. Return only valid JSON that conforms to the provided schema.\n\n- Inputs:\n  - PRIORITIZATION_RULES: A structured description of:\n    - Signals to look for in an opportunity (names, detection logic, and any evidence extraction guidance).\n    - Scoring logic (weights per signal and any thresholds).\n    - Classification thresholds mapping numeric score to status buckets.\n  - Extracted data: The rules also include or reference the extracted signals/evidence from the document.\n  - Opportunity Data : {{$context.$nodes.CONSOLIDATE_ALL_OUTPUT.$output.result}}\n\n- Source of rules and signals:\n  - Use the variable: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_THE_PRIORITIZATION_RULES.$output.value}} \n\n- Defaulting behavior:\n  - If a signal’s weight is missing, default it to 1.0.\n  - If a normalization factor or max score is missing, assume the total possible score is the sum of available (or defaulted) weights.\n  - If classification thresholds are missing, use these defaults:\n    - 0–24 → Low\n    - 25–49 → Medium\n    - 50–74 → High\n    - 75–100 → Critical\n  - If more than 3 strong signals are available, select the top 3 by impact on the score.\n\n- Scoring method (apply unless rules explicitly provide a different method):\n  1) Identify which signals are present from the extracted content described in PRIORITIZATION_RULES. Each signal has:\n     - name\n     - presence or intensity (derive from the evidence if provided)\n     - optional weight\n  2) For binary signals (present/absent): contribution = weight if present, else 0.\n     For graded signals (e.g., Low/Med/High/Critical): map to multipliers {Low: 0.25, Medium: 0.5, High: 0.75, Critical: 1.0} unless rules specify otherwise. contribution = weight × multiplier.\n  3) Sum contributions across all considered signals to get rawScore.\n  4) Compute maxPossible as the sum of weights (or defaulted weights). If using graded signals, assume the maximum multiplier is 1.0.\n  5) Normalize to 0–100: priotizationScore = round( (rawScore / maxPossible) × 100 ).\n  6) Determine priotizationStatus via thresholds from rules; otherwise use the default thresholds above.\n\n- Selecting “signals” field:\n  - Return 1–3 signals with the strongest impact on the final score.\n  - For each:\n    - name: exact signal name from rules.\n    - priotizationLevel: map presence/intensity to one of [\"Low\",\"Medium\",\"High\",\"Critical\"]. If binary present/absent, use “High” for present unless rules suggest another mapping; use “Low” if absent but referenced as influential in rationale.\n    - evidence: a concise phrase (≤ 50 chars) quoting or summarizing the supporting snippet. If no direct quote is allowed or available, summarize briefly and factually.\n\n- Rational field:\n  - Provide 1–3 ultra-concise bullets (each ≤ 3 words) capturing why the score/classification was assigned (e.g., “Tight deadline”, “High budget”, “C-level sponsor”).\n\n- Output requirements:\n  - Return only JSON with no additional text.\n  - Must strictly follow the provided JSON Schema:\n\n- Validation and safety:\n  - Do not fabricate signals or evidence; only use what is indicated or derivable from PRIORITIZATION_RULES and extracted content.\n  - If rules conflict, prioritize explicit numeric weights and thresholds over heuristics.\n  - If insufficient information exists to score, assume absent signals (score 0 for them) and proceed with defaults.\n\n- Example reasoning pattern (do not include in output):\n  - Identify signals present, map to levels, apply weights (default 1.0 if missing), sum, normalize to 100, classify using thresholds, pick top 1–3 signals, craft brief evidence and 1–3 word rational items, return JSON only."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n      \"title\": \"Opportunity Summary\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"priotizationScore\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100 },\n        \"priotizationStatus\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\", \"Critical\"] },\n        \"signals\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"maxItems\": 3,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": false,\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Signal name\" },\n              \"priotizationLevel\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\", \"Critical\"] },\n              \"evidence\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 50 }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"name\", \"priotizationLevel\", \"evidence\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"rational\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"maxItems\": 3,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Detailed rationale for the summary and recommendations\",\n            \"maxLength\": 3\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"priotizationScore\", \"priotizationStatus\", \"signals\", \"rational\"]\n    }",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
